    "durationMs": 504319,
    "finalText": "The implementation is complete and verified. Final state:\n\n- **Stack**: Laravel 11 / PHP 8.3 / MySQL 8.4 (`bench` DB) — credentials read only from `DB_*` env vars (removed `DB_CONNECTION=sqlite` from `.env`).\n- **Persistence**: `links` table migration (unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, `id` for creation order); clicks use atomic `increment()`. Verified data and counts survive a server restart.\n- **Routes** in `routes/api.php` registered with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`, so paths are `/links`, `/links/{code}`, `/r/{code}`.\n- **Responses**: 201 create (auto-generated 8-char code when omitted), 409 duplicate code, 200 show/list (items ascending by id, integer `clicks`), 302 redirect with exact `Location` + one increment, 404/422 with `error` field via exception render hooks (malformed JSON → empty input → 422).\n- **URL validation**: parse_url-based — requires http/https scheme, non-empty host, no whitespace; code validated against `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`.\n- **`start.sh`** (executable): runs `php artisan migrate --force`, then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload`; works from any cwd. README documents `sh start.sh`.\n\nI exercised every endpoint and edge case (boundaries, nulls, non-string code, uppercase scheme, unknown codes, malformed JSON), ran `php artisan test` (2 passed), then stopped my server, freed port 8000, and truncated test rows so the suite starts clean."
